      "reason": "The ~0.62 ns dominating this 0.94 ns path is the combinational equality decode of cycle_counter qualified by fsm_state that generates next_bit; it lives just above the counter block and can be pre-computed against CYCLES_PER_BIT-1 and registered for zero added latency, whereas my scope contains only the launch flop and an adder that is off the path."
